---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Visa | PGNX</title>
	</head>
	<body class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-b from-white via-green-50 to-white text-gray-900 relative">

	<div
		class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 -z-10"
		style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #16653440 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 24px 24px;"
	></div>
	<div class="pointer-events-none fixed left-1/2 top-40 -z-10 h-[500px] w-[500px] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-green-300 opacity-20 blur-3xl"></div>

	<img
		src="/logo.jpg"
		alt=""
		class="pointer-events-none fixed left-1/2 top-1/2 -z-10 h-[600px] w-[600px] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full object-cover opacity-5 grayscale"
	/>

		<!-- Top bar -->
		<header class="w-full py-4 px-6 flex items-center justify-between">
			<a href="/" class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
				<img src="/logo.jpg" alt="PGNX logo" class="h-20 w-20 rounded-full object-cover border border-green-100" />
				<span class="text-sm font-bold text-green-800">PGNX</span>
			</a>
		</header>

		<!-- Side menu toggle tab -->
		<button
			id="menu-toggle"
			class="fixed left-0 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 z-40 flex flex-col items-center gap-2 rounded-r-xl bg-green-800 text-white px-2 py-5 [writing-mode:vertical-rl]"
		>
			<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="[writing-mode:horizontal-tb] rotate-90">
				<path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/>
				<path d="M9 22V12h6v10"/>
			</svg>
			HOME
		</button>

		<!-- Slide-out side menu -->
		<nav
			id="side-menu"
			class="fixed left-0 top-0 h-full w-64 -translate-x-full bg-green-900 text-white p-6 transition-transform duration-300 z-50"
		>
			<button id="menu-close" class="mb-6 text-sm text-green-200">&#10005; Close</button>
			<ul class="space-y-4 font-medium">
				<li><a href="/" class="hover:text-green-300">Home</a></li>
				<li><a href="/admission" class="hover:text-green-300">Admission</a></li>
				<li><a href="/visa" class="hover:text-green-300">Visa</a></li>
				<li><a href="/resources" class="hover:text-green-300">Resources</a></li>
				<li><a href="/about" class="hover:text-green-300">About Us</a></li>
				<li><a href="/contact" class="hover:text-green-300">Contact</a></li>
			</ul>
		</nav>

		<!-- Main content -->
		<main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">

			<a href="/" class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:text-green-900">&larr; Back to Home</a>

			<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-extrabold text-green-800">Student Visa for Germany</h1>
			<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">What the German student visa actually involves — the process, and what to expect.</p>

			<!-- Overview -->
			<section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-800">General Overview</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Once you've secured admission at a German university, the next step is applying for a
					<strong> study visa</strong> to enter Germany. This is done through the consular services
					portal of your designated German consulate — either the <strong>German Embassy in
					Islamabad</strong> or the <strong>German Consulate General in Karachi</strong>, depending
					on where you're from.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					As a general rule, applicants from <strong>Sindh and Balochistan</strong> apply through the
					Karachi consulate, while applicants from <strong>Punjab, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,
					Gilgit-Baltistan, and Azad Jammu &amp; Kashmir</strong> apply through the Islamabad embassy.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-green-50 border border-green-100 p-4 text-sm text-green-800">
					<strong>Important:</strong> Visa appointment waiting times are usually long, so start your
					application as early as possible and have everything ready in advance.
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Application Process -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-800">Application Process</h2>
				<ol class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-gray-700">
					<li><strong>1. Create an account</strong> on the consular services portal of your designated consulate.</li>
					<li><strong>2. Complete and submit your application</strong>, then join the waiting list.</li>
					<li><strong>3. Wait to be notified.</strong> Waiting times vary and can take a while, so patience is key here.</li>
					<li><strong>4. Document verification.</strong> Once the embassy verifies your submitted documents, they'll send you a link to book your appointment.</li>
					<li><strong>5. Attend your appointment</strong> at your designated consulate on the scheduled date.</li>
					<li><strong>6. Wait for the decision</strong> on your visa application.</li>
				</ol>
				<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-green-50 border border-green-100 p-4 text-sm text-green-800">
					<strong>Note:</strong> Visa requirements and processing times can change. Always confirm
					current details on your designated consulate's official website before applying.
				</div>
			</section>

		</main>

		<!-- Footer -->
		<footer class="mt-12 border-t border-green-100 py-6 px-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm text-gray-500 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
			<p>&copy; 2025 PGNX &mdash; Pakistan Germany Nexus. All rights reserved.</p>
			<div class="flex gap-4">
				<a href="#" aria-label="Facebook" class="hover:text-green-700">FB</a>
				<a href="#" aria-label="Instagram" class="hover:text-green-700">IG</a>
				<a href="#" aria-label="WhatsApp" class="hover:text-green-700">WA</a>
			</div>
		</footer>

		<script>
			const toggle = document.getElementById("menu-toggle");
			const menu = document.getElementById("side-menu");
			const close = document.getElementById("menu-close");

			toggle?.addEventListener("click", () => {
				menu?.classList.remove("-translate-x-full");
			});
			close?.addEventListener("click", () => {
				menu?.classList.add("-translate-x-full");
			});
		</script>
	</body>
</html>